# SPDX-License-Identifier: CeCILL-2.1 OR AGPL-3.0-or-later
# Windows (Rtools45 / mingw-w64, UCRT) link line for the C glue over the prebuilt
# nirs4all-io-capi staticlib. The capi is built with the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu
# toolchain (see build_and_test.sh) so its ABI matches Rtools' mingw gcc, which
# performs the final link of the Rust archive into nirs4allio.dll.
#
# Two reasons the default `-lnirs4all_io_capi + (nothing)` from src/Makevars fails
# here, both fixed below:
#
# 1. R's gcc driver — not rustc — drives the link, so it does NOT auto-append the
#    Rust-std native system libs. Add the exact `rustc --print native-static-libs`
#    set for x86_64-pc-windows-gnu (kernel32 ntdll userenv ws2_32 dbghelp) plus
#    -lgcc for the panic_unwind EH/personality + __chkstk refs. NOTE: Rtools45's
#    mingw ships NO separate libgcc_eh.a — the unwinder (_Unwind_*),
#    __gcc_personality_seh0, and __chkstk are all merged into libgcc.a, so -lgcc
#    (not -lgcc_eh) is the one that resolves them here. (std is precompiled with
#    panic=unwind; panic="abort" cannot drop it on stable Rust without nightly
#    -Z build-std.) The rest of the mingw CRT tail (-lmsvcrt/-lmingwex/-lmingw32)
#    is supplied by Rtools' gcc driver itself — do NOT duplicate it here (Rtools45
#    is UCRT; forcing -lmsvcrt would mismatch the CRT).
#    System libs MUST come AFTER the archive (mingw ld is order-sensitive).
#
# 2. Reference the staticlib by EXACT PATH, not `-lnirs4all_io_capi`. build_and_test.sh
#    builds only the staticlib (libnirs4all_io_capi.a) on Windows, so the explicit
#    .a path forces the static link and all symbols land inside nirs4allio.dll
#    (Windows has no rpath, so a self-contained DLL is what we want).
PKG_CPPFLAGS = -I$(N4IO_INCLUDE)
PKG_LIBS = $(N4IO_CAPI_DIR)/libnirs4all_io_capi.a \
  -lkernel32 -lntdll -luserenv -lws2_32 -ldbghelp -lgcc
